// REAL schema, confirmed live from the Eventstream's auto-generated ingestion
// mapping (`.show table BusTelemetryRaw ingestion mappings`) — NOT the
// invented custom schema from the design doc. The built-in "Buses" sample is
// a real public-transit on-time-performance feed: Timestamp, TripId, BusLine,
// StationNumber, ScheduleTime, plus a nested Properties bag. It does NOT
// emit engine temperature or battery telemetry — those were narrative
// flavor for a hypothetical custom feed, not something this sample provides.
//
// Properties' real shape, confirmed from live data: just two fields —
// BusState ("InMotion" observed so far) and TimeToNextStation (a timespan
// ETA to the next stop). No Latitude/Longitude/SpeedKph/OccupancyPercent
// anywhere in this sample — those columns stay permanently null for Buses
// sample data; they're not a hedge pending confirmation anymore, they're
// confirmed absent. TimeToNextStationSeconds is a genuinely useful signal
// this sample DOES provide: a vehicle whose TimeToNextStation isn't
// decreasing across consecutive readings while BusState stays "InMotion" is
// a real stall signal, arguably better than a fictional SpeedKph would have
// been.
//
// DelayMinutes is computed directly from Timestamp vs ScheduleTime (arrival
// vs. schedule) rather than trusting an invented field — this is real
// schedule-adherence data, arguably a better delay signal than what the
// design doc imagined.
//
// IngestionTime uses now(), not ingestion_time() — a live 400 confirmed that
// ingestion_time() is rejected in a *transactional* update policy on a source
// table that has streaming ingestion enabled (the error's own suggested fix
// was to disable streaming ingestion, which is the wrong tradeoff here: this
// project's whole point is real-time telemetry, so streaming ingestion stays
// on). now() is the update policy's execution time, which for a transactional
// policy is effectively ingestion time anyway — close enough for the
// Operations Agent's staleness watermark, without the restriction.
.create-or-alter function FlattenBusTelemetry() {
    BusTelemetryRaw
    | extend
        EventTime = Timestamp,
        VehicleId = TripId,
        RouteId = BusLine,
        Latitude = real(null),              // not provided by the built-in Buses sample
        Longitude = real(null),             // not provided by the built-in Buses sample
        SpeedKph = real(null),              // not provided by the built-in Buses sample
        EngineTemperatureC = real(null),    // not provided by the built-in Buses sample
        BatteryPercent = real(null),        // not provided by the built-in Buses sample
        DelayMinutes = toreal(datetime_diff('minute', Timestamp, ScheduleTime)),
        OccupancyPercent = real(null),       // not provided by the built-in Buses sample
        Status = tostring(Properties.BusState),
        TimeToNextStationSeconds = toreal(totimespan(Properties.TimeToNextStation) / 1s),
        IngestionTime = now()
    // Column order here must match the TABLE's physical column order, not
    // reading order — .create-merge appends new columns to the end of an
    // already-existing table's schema (Kusto's documented behavior), so
    // TimeToNextStationSeconds (added after IngestionTime already existed)
    // comes last here too, confirmed by a live schema-mismatch 400 otherwise.
    | project EventTime, VehicleId, RouteId, Latitude, Longitude, SpeedKph, EngineTemperatureC,
        BatteryPercent, DelayMinutes, OccupancyPercent, Status, IngestionTime, TimeToNextStationSeconds
}

.alter table BusTelemetry policy update
'''[{"IsEnabled": true, "Source": "BusTelemetryRaw", "Query": "FlattenBusTelemetry()", "IsTransactional": true, "PropagateIngestionProperties": false}]'''
